# ABOUTME: libFuzzer dictionary for Http3StreamFuzz: whole operations of its input encoding (stream
# ABOUTME: types, frames, QPACK instructions) and raw HTTP/3 frame and QPACK field-line bytes.
# control stream type on uni stream 2
"\x00\x00\x00\x00"
# QPACK encoder and decoder stream types
"\x00\x01\x00\x02"
"\x00\x02\x00\x03"
# SETTINGS frame on uni stream 2: QPACK capacity 0, field section 4096
"\x01\x00\x00\x02\x02\x00\x00\x01\x03"
# GOAWAY, MAX_PUSH_ID, CANCEL_PUSH frames
"\x01\x00\x00\x03\x02"
"\x01\x00\x00\x04\x04"
"\x01\x00\x00\x05\x00"
# request HEADERS GET https://localhost/ with FIN
"\x04\x00\x80\x01\x04\x00\x0c\x10\x29\x05"
# request DATA, 5 bytes in 3-byte reads
"\x04\x00\x03\x00\x00\x05"
# FIN on request stream 0, reset of uni stream 2
"\x07\x80"
"\x03\x00"
# raw frames: SETTINGS empty, GOAWAY 0, DATA empty, HEADERS empty section, grease type
"\x04\x00"
"\x07\x01\x00"
"\x00\x00"
"\x01\x02\x00\x00"
"\x21\x00"
# raw QPACK field lines: :method GET, :path /, :scheme https, :authority localhost
"\xd1"
"\xc1"
"\xd7"
"\x50\x09localhost"
# QPACK encoder / decoder instructions: capacity 0, section ack, increment, cancellation
"\x20"
"\x81"
"\x01"
"\x41"
